@startuml User Deletion Guard (Lab 3)

actor Client
participant "Gateway" as GW
participant "User Service" as US
participant "Order Service" as OS
participant "RabbitMQ" as MQ
participant "Notification Service" as NS

== Scenario 1: User with Open Orders (409 Conflict) ==

Client -> GW: DELETE /users/{userId}
GW -> US: Forward request
US -> US: Find user by ID

US -> OS: GET /orders/users/{userId}/open-exists\n(Synchronous HTTP)
OS -> OS: Check if user has orders\nwith status "CREATED"
OS --> US: {"exists": true}

US -> US: User has open orders\nCANNOT DELETE
US --> GW: 409 Conflict\n{"message": "User has open orders"}
GW --> Client: 409 Conflict

note over US, OS
  **Synchronous Communication**
  User Service queries Order Service
  to check for open orders before deletion
end note

== Scenario 2: User without Orders (204 No Content) ==

Client -> GW: DELETE /users/{userId}
GW -> US: Forward request
US -> US: Find user by ID

US -> OS: GET /orders/users/{userId}/open-exists\n(Synchronous HTTP)
OS -> OS: Check if user has orders\nwith status "CREATED"
OS --> US: {"exists": false}

US -> US: No open orders\nPROCEED with deletion
US -> US: Delete user from DB
US -> MQ: Publish "user.deleted" event
US --> GW: 204 No Content
GW --> Client: 204 No Content

MQ --> NS: Consume "user.deleted"
NS -> NS: Delete all notifications\nfor this user
NS -> NS: Save changes to DB

note over US
  **Guard Logic:**
  1. Check open orders (sync)
  2. If exists → 409
  3. If not → delete + publish event
end note

note over OS
  **"Open Orders" Definition:**
  Orders with status = "CREATED"
  (Configurable in future)
end note

@enduml
